  "notes": "WORD FORMATION:\n{顕|けん} (manifest, apparent) + {在|ざい} (exist). Literally \"existing in a visible way.\"\n\nUSAGE:\nOften used in the form {顕在化|けんざいか}する (to become manifest). Common in news, academic writing, and business contexts when discussing problems, risks, or trends that were previously hidden.\n\nANTONYM:\n- {潜在|せんざい}: latent, potential, hidden\n\nHOMOPHONES:\n- {健在|けんざい}: alive and well, in good health\n- {建材|けんざい}: building materials\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {顕在化|けんざいか}する: to become manifest\n- {問題|もんだい}が{顕在化|けんざいか}する: problems become apparent\n- {顕在的|けんざいてき}: actual, manifest (adjective form)",
